# Text is stored with LF. Scripts and Dockerfiles keep LF in a Windows checkout
# as well, so that checkout can be mounted into the Dockerfile.cross container
# and run there; and git in that container, which has no core.autocrlf, then
# sees the other files as unchanged instead of modified (scripts/release.sh
# refuses a dirty tree).
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
# Binary data: the fuzz seed corpora, the compiled checkpoints and the test
# wallets. Git's own guess gets these right today, but a short input with no
# control bytes would be taken for text and have its line endings rewritten.
*.bin binary
*.wallet binary
